":"Particle Count and Size Analyzer","Mapped Term Ontology":"ncit","Match Type":"SEARCH_RESULT","Score":0.75,"Short Form":"NCIT_C62330","Source":"Zooma","Zooma Confidence":"GOOD"},{"Class Definition":"Gel permeation or sieve chromatography that is performed on porous gels that separate solutes on the basis of size. Smaller solutes are included within the particles of the gel matrix more frequently than larger solutes, thus affecting elution rates.","Class Name":"Gel Filtration Chromatography","Detailed Ontology":"ncit","Is Defining Ontology":true,"Mapped Term IRI":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C16433","Mapped Term Label":"Gel Filtration Chromatography","Mapped Term Ontology":"ncit","Match Type":"SEARCH_RESULT","Score":0.5,"Short Form":"NCIT_C16433","Source":"Zooma","Zooma Confidence":"MEDIUM"},{"Class Definition":"In sizing columns (gel filtration), the elution position of a protein or of a complex depends on its Stokes radius. Molecules with a radius that is smaller than the bead size are retained and retarded by the interaction with the matrix. The observation that two proteins, loaded on a sieving column, elute in a fraction(s) corresponding to a MW that is larger than the MW of either protein may be taken as an indication that the two proteins interact. Furthermore this technique provides a conceptually simple method for evaluating the affinity of the interaction.","Class Name":"molecular sieving","Detailed Ontology":"mi","Is Defining Ontology":true,"Mapped Term IRI":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MI_0071","Mapped Term Label":"molecular sieving","Mapped Term Ontology":"mi","Match Type":"SEARCH_RESULT","Score":0.5,"Short Form":"MI_0071","Source":"Zooma","Zooma Confidence":"MEDIUM"},{"Class Definition":"Information about the size of the device that is not represented elsewhere.","Class Name":"Device Size Text","Detailed Ontology":"ncit","Is Defining Ontology":true,"Mapped Term IRI":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C106041","Mapped Term Label":"Device S